bridge/pull/24) — WARN-log demote + per-remote `DiagnosticStatus` (merged 2026-05-21)\n- *(stretch)* [`rolker/unh_marine_perception#6`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/6) — `SeaSurfaceLayer::matchSize` segfault — another agent in flight; passively poll\n\n## Hosts active\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub + boat compute)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (only if a survey phase is reached)\n- **dev** — workspace dev machine (this agent)\n\n## Day plan\n\n### Block 1 — Pre-power wrap-ups (~09:30 → ~10:30 EDT, dev-side)\n\n- [ ] Land the three remaining must-merge prereq PRs (other agents driving — coordinate, don't duplicate):\n  - PR #146 — Remove `diagnostic_aggregator`\n  - PR #147 — `output='both'` in launches\n  - `ros2_network_monitor` PR #24 — startup-connect hardening\n- [ ] Stage FCU param diff as a committed artifact at `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/2026-05-21_ek3_z_source_reconfig.parm` so gabby agent has a single file to load (not a freehand edit).\n- [ ] `make sync` once more right before powering on, so each host has the latest jazzy.\n\n### Block 2 — Pre-launch (~10:30 → ~11:30 EDT, boat powered, on cart)\n\n**FCU param ground truth** (verified against `bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param` and `_baseline.param`). CUAV-on-Cube is the primary nav; SBG is payload-only:\n\n| Param | Currently on boat | Target | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `EK3_SRC1_POSZ` | `1` (baro) | `3` (GPS) | Stops EKF Z tracking atmospheric pressure |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_X` | (unset → 0) | `0.835` | CUAV forward antenna X (m), ahead of `base_link` |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_Y` | (unset → 0) | `0.000` | Centerline |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_Z` | (unset → 0) | `-0.890` | CUAV antenna 0.89 m above `base_link` (ArduPilot: negative = up) |\n| `GPS_POS1_X / Y / Z` | `0.835 / 0.000 / -0.890` | unchanged | Already correct from #91 |\n\nOrder matters — FCU reconfig **before** ROS bring-up so the EKF behavior is observed from clean boot.\n\n- [ ] FCU param load via QGC (gabby agent at the dock).\n- [ ] Cube reboot; wait for EKF home set + GPS lock.\n- [ ] Verify the 4 changed params stuck (`param show EK3_SRC1_POSZ EK3_GPS_OFFS_X EK3_GPS_OFFS_Y EK3_GPS_OFFS_Z`).\n- [ ] Bring up ROS on gabby; check no startup crashes (with #147 in, ERROR logs should land in `~/.ros/log/`).\n- [ ] **Quick sanity on FCU reconfig effect** (boat still on cart, in view of the sky):\n  - `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/mavros/global_position/global -n 1` → Z should now be plausibly near the SBG MSL+undulation chart-datum range, not the previous ~−12 m.\n  - `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/tide_estimate -n 1` → should land inside the plausibility band, no `sea_surface_estimator` suppression warnings.\n- [ ] Operator-side bring-up (salmon):\n  - Annunciator clean (no `bencloud` key after #148, no STALE `/Operator/*` buckets after #146 if merged, `/diagnostics_agg` absent).\n  - Ping monitor: gabby / router / DNS all green from baseline.\n- [ ] **`ros2_network_monitor#24` validation** (operator-side, dockside before launch): briefly pull boat-router power or block its address for ~30 s. Confirm monitor stays alive and publishes `(attempt N, retry in Xs)`; restore and confirm normal resume.\n- [ ] **RC mode switch** to AUTO/GUIDED before autonomous segments (per the fringe-range carry-forward — see Cautions).\n- [ ] Go/no-go decision; launch.\n\n### Block 3 — In-water mission (~11:30 → 14:00 EDT, ~2.5 h)\n\nSequenced in priority order. **Cut from the bottom if time slips.** Current at Clark Island (ACT0731 bin 1) is near slack at 12:01 EDT and builds to ~1.5 kt flood @ 270° by 14:03 — manageable but plan accordingly.\n\n| # | Phase | What | Duration | Pass criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Bring-up confirm | Stationary near pier; verify `map → map_tide` TF, `sea_surface_estimator` stable | ~10 min | TF resolved with sane Z; 0 suppression warnings in fresh log |\n| 1 | FCU reconfig validation | Short trackline (e.g. 100 m × 3 legs) at low speed near slack | ~30 min | Nav stack stable; `mavros/global_position/*` Z chart-datum-compatible; body-frame SBG−MAV offset drops toward GPS-CEP (sub-decimeter ideally), not the 0.64 m steady offset documented in #111 |\n| 2 | `udp_bridge#24` WARN demote | Take boat to 300–500 m WiFi-only, then a brief Starlink-only segment | ~30 min | Per-event WARN volume orders-of-magnitude reduced from 27,992-in-2h baseline (2026-05-19); per-remote `DiagnosticStatus` shows give-up rate |\n| 3 | `#147` ERROR-log capture | Mid-mission, deliberately kill one node on gabby; confirm crash/ERROR landed in the session log file | ~5 min | ERROR text present in `~/.ros/log/\u003csession\u003e/` for the affected node |\n| 4 | *(stretch)* perception #6 | Only if a PR landed pre-launch and bench-tested; enable `SeaSurfaceLayer` in local costmap and run a short trackline | ~20 min | `controller_server` stays up; no segfault; costmap shows non-water classification reaching it |\n| 5 | *(stretch)* bandwidth segment | Brief Starlink-only segment at moderate distance, recording bag | ~15 min | Bag captures a clean Starlink-only window for offline analysis |\n\n**Hard stop: all surface activity ends by 14:00 EDT.** Recovery to dock + power down to clear the 14:30 departure.\n\n### Block 4 — Wrap-up (async, post-departure)\n\n- Field hosts push their logs to gitcloud at end of session.\n- Dev pulls field logs into the worktree branch.\n- Dev integrates brief one-sentence summaries of significant field-agent entries into the dev log's Timeline (`gabby agent (gabby log §N): …`).\n- Audit for carry-forward; open follow-up task issues; update `docs/roadmap.md` with anything deferred.\n- Wrap-up PR closing #149 — done by dev side later today or next morning, per the iterative-PR pattern.\n\n## Logs\n\n- [`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-21_dev_logs.md`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/feature/issue-149/docs/logs/2026/2026-05-21_dev_logs.md) — dev (this agent)\n- *(gabby / salmon / mercat per-host files appear here as their agents initialize them)*\n\n## Carry-forward cautions\n\n- **RC mode-switch at fringe range** — FCU honors RC channel even with `FS_THR_ENABLE=0`. Pin RC mode switch to AUTO/GUIDED or power off the controller before autonomous segments.\n- **BT `SkipUnknownTaskType` catchall** — [`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#25`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/25) filed but not yet fixed; a survey-line abort silently marks the line done. Be alert for hover-and-quit.\n- **mavros `/global` Z drift** — known ~5 m/hour drift WITHOUT the #138 reconfig. Today's reconfig should eliminate this; the chart-datum chain can come off the field-revert workaround once a deployment confirms.\n- **gitcloud reconciliation** — don't `git pull gitcloud main` to local main on github-origin repos. Reconcile via PR post-deployment.\n\n## Wrap-up checklist\n\n- [ ] Field hosts push logs to gitcloud\n- [ ] Dev pulls field logs into worktree branch\n- [ ] Dev integrates field-agent timeline entries into dev log\n- [ ] Audit for carry-forward; open follow-up task issues for anything bounded\n- [ ] Update `docs/roadmap.md` with anything deferred (not bounded enough to be a focused issue)\n- [ ] Open wrap-up PR closing #149\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1779372018,"nonce":"xljhcvVdrrbSkGTuxy3VEeXdXO0=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABC7EYUM69DxdT"},"target":"7d5b52c2c7b225990e98f39b9236ec7fa022ba1793b3df6b8808a427a14a9d20","message":"## Scope today\n\nValidate the small-wins prereqs batch + the already-merged `udp_bridge#24`\nWARN demote in a single short deployment, and apply the FCU EK3 Z-source\nreconfig from #138 as the primary upgrade for the day.\n\n- Hard stop on the water at **14:00 EDT** for boat recovery; Roland departs 14:30.\n- FCU reconfig (#138) goes in before launch — the validation needs it from clean boot.\n- Percep